    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0299" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg237"/>

                <head>No. 165.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pierrepont to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 15, 1877</date>.
                        (Received December 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of the 11th of
                    July last, introducing Mr. D. B. Eaton as chairman of the civil-service
                    commission, and handed to <pb facs="0300" n="238" xml:id="pg238"/> me in person
                    by that gentleman, I have now the honor to inclose to you a copy of a
                    communication addressed to Lord Tenterden by the lords commissioners of the
                    treasury, which is in answer to some inquiries of Mr. Eaton respecting the civil
                    service of Great Britain. I also inclose a copy of Lord Derby’s note,
                    transmitting the same to me.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARDS PIERREPONT.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d170-a1.xml" xpointer="d170-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d170-a2.xml" xpointer="d170-a2"/>
